item.text:
**Reused evidence**
- No prior evidence item was reused at the 7B personal-nexus standard. Earlier chapter material on Germany's institutions and general corruption context was treated as context only, not as proof of Scholz's personal honesty or dishonesty.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Scholz sieht keine politische Einflussnahme im Cum-Ex-Skandal","publisher":"Deutschlandfunk","publication_date":"2022-08-12","url":"https://www.deutschlandfunk.de/scholz-sieht-keine-politische-einflussnahme-im-cum-ex-skandal-106.html","claim":"At the summer press conference, Scholz said that after about 2.5 years of investigation there were no findings that he had politically influenced the Cum-Ex affair, and he again denied such influence.","locator":"article lead and first paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct report of Scholz's own public statement by a major public broadcaster; not a transcript, but close to the original remarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 public statement about earlier Hamburg conduct","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Scholz's own statement as chancellor.","contrary_evidence":["Later testimony and reporting continued to dispute his memory claims and the completeness of his account."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Scholz vor Cum-Ex-Ausschuss: \"Habe keinen Einfluss genommen\"","publisher":"tagesschau.de","publication_date":"2022-08-19","url":"https://www.tagesschau.de/inland/scholz-cum-ex-105.html","claim":"In his second appearance before the Hamburg inquiry, Scholz denied any influence on the Warburg tax procedure and said he still could not remember the contents of the meetings.","locator":"lead, first two paragraphs, and the section headed \"Weiterhin keine Erinnerung\"","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Public-broadcaster reporting of a live parliamentary hearing with direct quotations and procedural context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 testimony about 2016-2017 conduct","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal testimony by Scholz about his own conduct and memory.","contrary_evidence":["The committee continued because new documents and prior contradictions kept the issue open."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Grilling over Scholz's handling of multibillion-euro tax fraud ends in stand-off","publisher":"Reuters / Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-19","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/germanys-scholz-to-testify-over-handling-of-multibillioneuro-tax-fraud-2876122","claim":"Reuters reported that Scholz denied impropriety in the Warburg affair while opposition lawmakers accused him of obfuscating the truth, and the hearing ended without resolution.","locator":"headline and opening paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire copy is strong for event reporting and attribution, though the host page is a republish.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 hearing about earlier Hamburg conduct","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Scholz's own answers and the reactions they triggered.","contrary_evidence":["No court finding of deliberate lying was reported in this item; it records allegations and a stalemate rather than a legal conclusion."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Cum-Ex-Skandal: Versteckspiel im Kanzleramt","publisher":"tagesschau.de","publication_date":"2022-09-16","url":"https://www.tagesschau.de/investigativ/ndr-wdr/cum-ex-hamburg-warburg-bank-scholz-kahrs-101.html","claim":"Investigative reporting said a previously unknown calendar entry pointed to another meeting between Scholz and Johannes Kahrs and raised the question whether the meeting had been concealed.","locator":"middle section discussing the calendar entry and the newly surfaced meeting","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Investigative public-broadcaster report based on contemporaneous records and source reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 reporting about 2020 and earlier meetings relevant to Scholz's 2022 testimony","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Scholz's recorded meetings and his office's handling of the chronology.","contrary_evidence":["Scholz and Tschentscher denied political influence, and the article does not itself prove intentional concealment."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7","7B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gericht fordert Scholz zu Auskünften auf: Cum-Ex-Affäre erreicht Kanzleramt","publisher":"Tagesspiegel","publication_date":"2022-07-07","url":"https://www.tagesspiegel.de/politik/cum-ex-affare-erreicht-kanzleramt-scholz-schweigen-sagt-etwas-531234.html","claim":"The Berlin administrative court ordered the Chancellery to provide information about Scholz's personal knowledge from a confidential background conversation in the Cum-Ex matter, in response to a press-access dispute that included an allegation he had lied.","locator":"article body, opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong contemporaneous reporting of a specific court order and its factual basis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 legal scrutiny of Scholz's conduct and public-accountability duties","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Scholz's personal knowledge and the Chancellery's response to inquiry.","contrary_evidence":["This was a procedural order, not a finding that Scholz lied or acted corruptly."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Oberverwaltungsgericht gegen Auskunftspflicht: Scholz muss sich keinen Journalistenfragen zur Cum-Ex-Affäre stellen","publisher":"Tagesspiegel","publication_date":"2022-07-14","url":"https://www.tagesspiegel.de/politik/scholz-muss-sich-keinen-journalistenfragen-zur-cum-ex-affare-stellen-4347454.html","claim":"The higher administrative court reversed the earlier order and held that the Chancellery did not have to answer questions about matters with no service-related link to its own duties.","locator":"headline and second paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting of a specific appellate ruling with clear procedural effect.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"2022 appellate review of the same disclosure dispute","ruler_attribution":"Directly concerns the Chancellery's legal position under Scholz, but the ruling is about disclosure scope rather than truthfulness itself.","contrary_evidence":["The ruling limited disclosure obligations; it did not resolve the underlying truthfulness allegation."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Alle Fraktionen für Transparenz und Aufklärung bei Cum-Ex","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-10-13","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw41-de-aktuelle-stunde-warburg-915258","claim":"In a current-hour debate, all parliamentary groups called for full clarification of the Cum-Ex scandal and several speakers urged Scholz to contribute to the inquiry; the article also notes accusations that he had increasing memory lapses.","locator":"opening paragraphs and the section on new indications in the Cum-Ex case","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary record of floor proceedings and the arguments made there.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 parliamentary scrutiny of Scholz's earlier Hamburg conduct","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Scholz's conduct and his duty to help clarify the affair.","contrary_evidence":["SPD and Greens rejected claims of political influence, and the Bundestag record does not itself prove wrongdoing."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Neues Buch zur \"Cum Ex\"-Affäre: Protokolle nähren Zweifel an Erinnerungslücken von Scholz","publisher":"Tagesspiegel","publication_date":"2022-10-06","url":"https://www.tagesspiegel.de/politik/neues-buch-zur-cum-ex-affare-protokolle-nahren-zweifel-erinnerungslucken-von-olaf-scholz-8721487.html","claim":"A new book and the released committee protocols renewed doubts about Scholz's claimed memory lapses, because they suggested he had given more concrete recollections in earlier Bundestag testimony than he later acknowledged.","locator":"headline and opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Investigative newspaper report based on published protocols and pre-publication material; useful but still interpretive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 reporting on earlier testimony relevant to 2022 integrity scrutiny","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Scholz's own earlier testimony and later recall claims.","contrary_evidence":["The article frames the issue as a challenge to his memory narrative, not a legal finding of falsehood."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Olaf Scholz gibt Geheimprotokoll frei: Der Streit um die Kanzlerworte zu Cum-Ex","publisher":"Tagesspiegel","publication_date":"2022-12-22","url":"https://www.tagesspiegel.de/politik/olaf-scholz-gibt-geheimprotokoll-frei-der-streit-um-die-kanzlerworte-zu-cum-ex-9079459.html","claim":"The previously secret protocol of the Bundestag finance committee was circulated to MPs; the government said Scholz had not opposed publication and that the secrecy had been requested to protect tax confidentiality.","locator":"middle section on the release of the protocol and the government's explanation","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Strong reporting on a contested document release, but the article mixes direct reporting with political interpretation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 publication of records relevant to Scholz's 2020 testimony and 2022 scrutiny","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Scholz's handling of the protocol and the transparency dispute around his own remarks.","contrary_evidence":["Critics argued the protocol showed more recollection than Scholz admitted in Hamburg, so transparency did not settle the honesty question."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Cum-Ex-Skandal: Staatsanwaltschaft sieht von Ermittlungen gegen Olaf Scholz ab","publisher":"Sueddeutsche Zeitung","publication_date":"2022-08-16","url":"https://www.sueddeutsche.de/politik/cum-ex-scholz-tschentscher-generalstaatsanwaltschaft-1.5639733","claim":"Hamburg prosecutors rejected a complaint against Scholz and said there was no basis for opening an investigation into him over the Cum-Ex matter.","locator":"lead and first two paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Secondary reporting of a prosecutorial decision; reliable as context, but not a finding on the merits of integrity.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"2022 prosecutorial decision about Scholz's earlier conduct","ruler_attribution":"Directly concerns Scholz, but it is a no-prosecution decision rather than affirmative evidence of honesty.","contrary_evidence":["The decision declined to investigate; it does not affirm that the underlying conduct was clean or fully candid."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

The dossier is mixed and narrow. The strongest evidence cluster is the Cum-Ex/Warburg affair, where Scholz repeatedly denied influence, said he could not remember key details, and then faced sustained parliamentary and journalistic scrutiny over possible inconsistencies, concealed meetings, and disclosure disputes. The main favorable material is procedural: prosecutors declined to open a case, and a previously secret protocol was later released. I did not find direct 2022 evidence of self-enrichment, family profit, gifts, or nepotistic appointment of close associates.

**Search and rejection summary**
- Reviewed roughly 30 documents across Bundestag, Bundesregierung, Hamburg justice pages, Deutschlandfunk, tagesschau/ARD, Reuters, Tagesspiegel, SZ, WELT, Bloomberg, Guardian, and NDR.
- Kept only documents with a clear personal nexus to Scholz's own conduct, testimony, disclosure behavior, or the scrutiny of that conduct.
- Rejected duplicates that repeated the same hearing or the same newspaper piece with no new factual claim.
- Rejected out-of-period follow-ups from 2023-2024 unless they were only background for the 2022 record.
- Rejected generic Germany corruption/rule-of-law indicators as evidence; they remain context only.
- One major source family, Spiegel, was blocked by robots and not used.
- I also dropped broad cabinet/government-formation material because it did not rise to a direct integrity claim about Scholz personally.

**Remaining gaps**
- No direct evidence found on 7B.3 or 7B.4: personal/family/business profit, gifts, hidden assets, or financial self-dealing.
- No strong ruler-specific evidence on 7B.5 or 7B.9 beyond general cabinet formation and coalition governance; I did not find a 2022 item showing patronage or its absence with enough specificity.
- The 7B.6/7B.7 record is still mostly procedural and reputational, not a hard adjudication of dishonesty.
- A deeper pass on court records, parliamentary transcripts, and asset/conflict disclosures could help, but only if it turns up ruler-specific primary records rather than more commentary.
- If you want a stricter 7B pass, the next useful search would be on original Bundestag transcripts, Hamburg committee records, and any official disclosure or ethics filings tied to the Warburg/Cum-Ex episode.
